      "decision_index": 32,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The opponent's graveyard has 16 cards, which is close to the 20-card threshold for Visions of Beyond to draw 3 instead of 1. However, Gem3P Timmy has Oboro, Palace in the Clouds in hand and Ruin Crab on the battlefield. Playing Oboro would trigger Ruin Crab's landfall, milling the opponent for 3 more cards, bringing their graveyard to 19 cards. That's still not 20, so Visions would still only draw 1. But the correct sequence is: play Oboro (trigger Ruin Crab, mill 3, opponent GY goes to 19), then cast Visions of Beyond for 1 card draw. Even drawing 1 card is better than passing and doing nothing. More importantly, skipping the Visions of Beyond cast entirely wastes available mana and a card draw opportunity. The player has an untapped Watery Grave that can produce U, and after playing Oboro they'd have access to cast Visions. Even if it only draws 1 card, that's pure value with open mana. Skipping both the land drop AND the spell cast is a clear mistake - they should at minimum play Oboro to trigger Ruin Crab mill and use their mana for Visions of Beyond.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spells, skipping the opportunity to cast Visions of Beyond and missing a Ruin Crab landfall trigger from Oboro.",
