      "decision_index": 35,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The opponent's graveyard has 19 cards, just one short of the 20-card threshold for Visions of Beyond to draw 3 instead of 1. However, Visions of Beyond at end of opponent's turn would still draw 1 card at instant speed, which is fine timing. The real issue is that the player has an untapped Watery Grave and could cast Visions of Beyond at the end of the opponent's next turn instead, potentially after the graveyard reaches 20 cards (very likely with Ruin Crab triggers). But more importantly, the player chose to pass without playing Oboro, Palace in the Clouds. Playing Oboro would trigger Ruin Crab's landfall, milling the opponent for 3 more cards, pushing their graveyard to 22 cards. Then casting Visions of Beyond with the untapped Watery Grave would draw 3 cards instead of 1. This is a significant missed opportunity - playing a free land to trigger landfall mill AND enable a 3-card draw instead of a 1-card draw.",
