      "description": "The opponent's graveyard has 19 cards, which is just one short of the 20-card threshold for Visions of Beyond to draw 3 cards instead of 1. However, Ruin Crab is on the battlefield and the player has Oboro, Palace in the Clouds in hand - playing Oboro next turn will trigger Ruin Crab to mill 3 more cards, easily pushing the graveyard over 20. That said, casting Visions of Beyond right now during combat (before the opponent's end step) would only draw 1 card since the graveyard has exactly 19 cards. The real missed opportunity is casting Visions of Beyond at end of opponent's turn after the graveyard crosses 20 - but wait, it's the opponent's combat step right now and the graveyard is at 19. The player could cast Visions of Beyond for 1 card now, but waiting until they can trigger landfall with Oboro to get 3 cards is correct. Actually, looking more carefully - the opponent has 19 cards in graveyard. The player passed on both spells. Fatal Push has no valid target (no opponent creatures), so that's fine. For Visions of Beyond, waiting to draw 3 instead of 1 is reasonable if they plan to trigger Ruin Crab first. This is actually a reasonable pass.",
